# Scraped competitor price exports — private raw material, not a deliverable (2026-09-19).
# Named families only, never a blanket ignore for this folder: several files here are
# tracked on purpose (browser scrape scripts, manifest json, catalogue tree).
# Root .gitignore repeats these as defence in depth.

iam_sku_*.csv
iam_sku_*.json
ks_*.csv
ks_*.json
_ks_*.csv
_ks_*.json
oem_peer_*.csv
oem_peer_*.json
spareto_*.csv
spareto_*.json

# Price-list workbooks and priced master exports — private raw material, not a deliverable (2026-09-19).
# Named families only, by stem plus a required .xls* extension: a bare *.xls* here would be
# redundant with the root global workbook rule, would obscure which file it protects, and would
# sit over the tracked scrape scripts and json in this folder.
# Stems keep the real filename casing; .xls* covers .xls/.xlsx/.xlsm/.xlsb.
Price_file*.xls*
PRICE_CD*.xls*
CY2026_Price_Revision*.xls*
PR00_*.xls*
ZPR1_UPLOAD_LAYOUT_*.xls*
EXPORT_ZPR1*.xls*
parts_master*.xls*
pricing_simulation_*.xls*
spa2_*.xls*
UTI_final_price_file*.xls*
SAP_Pull_PN_Validity_List*.xls*
eucon_*.xls*
Eucon_*.xls*
# Bare 2023.xlsx (mixed PR00 + ZPR1). The stem is a year with no family word, so it is named
# on its own rather than reached with a wider pattern.
2023.xls*
